7150","title":"FAA TFR 6/7150 (security): NORTHWEST FIELD, GU (261113-261220 Guam MDA REISSUE)","tier":"routine","data_as_of":"2026-11-12T00:49:34Z","countries":["GU"],"precision_class":"area","ncf":["transport_by_air"],"sector":["transportation_systems"],"requirement_ids":["CD-PIR-7"],"ie_aspect":["physical"],"pmesii_pt":["infrastructure"],"ascope":["areas"],"sources":[{"id":"faa-tfr","publisher":"US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA)","url":"https://tfr.faa.gov/tfr3/?page=detail_6_7150","licence":"US Government work, not subject to US copyright (17 U.S.C. 105); the FAA states no licence on the TFR site","grade":"A1","independence_group":"faa","source_type":"official notice","descriptor":"Temporary flight restriction (NOTAM), with the FAA's own boundary","accessed_at":"2026-11-15T01:11:05Z"}],"link":"https://tfr.faa.gov/tfr3/?page=detail_6_7150","measures":{"notam_id":"6/7150","type":"SECURITY","new":false,"facility":"ZUA","state":"GU","description":"NORTHWEST FIELD, GU, Friday, November 13, 2026 through Sunday, December 20, 2026 Local","created":"11/12/2026","effective":"2026-11-12T22:00:00Z","issued":"2026-11-12T00:49:34Z","regulation":"99.7","floor":"500 ft MSL","ceiling":"12000 ft MSL","text":"!FDC 6/7150 ZUA GU..AIRSPACE NORTHWEST FIELD, GU..TEMPORARY FLIGHT RESTRICTIONS. NOVEMBER 13-DECEMBER 20, 2026 LOCAL. PURSUANT TO 49 USC 40103(B)(3), THE FEDERAL AVIATION ADMINISTRATION (FAA) CLASSIFIES THE AIRSPACE DEFINED IN THIS NOTAM AS 'NTL DEFENSE AIRSPACE'. ANY PERSON WHO KNOWINGLY OR WILLFULLY VIOLATES THE RULES CONCERNING OPS IN THIS AIRSPACE MAY BE SUBJECT TO CERTAIN CRIMINAL PENALTIES UNDER 49 USC SECTION 46307. PILOTS WHO DO NOT ADHERE TO THE FOLLOWING PROC MAY BE INTERCEPTED, DETAINED AND INTERVIEWED BY LAW ENFORCEMENT/SECURITY PERSONNEL. PURSUANT TO 14 CFR 99.7, SPECIAL SECURITY INSTRUCTIONS, ALL ACFT FLT OPS ARE PROHIBITED: WI AN AREA DEFINED AS 133709N1445205E (UNZ037012.6) TO 133859N1445156E (UNZ032014) THEN CLOCKWISE ON A 1.78NM ARC CENTERED ON 133709N1445205E (UNZ037012.6) TO 133725N1445356E (UNZ042014) TO POINT OF ORIGIN 500FT MSL-12000FT MSL EFFECTIVE 2611122200 UTC (0800 LOCAL 11/13/26) UNTIL 2611151300 UTC (2300 LOCAL 11/15/26) DLY 2200-1300 (0800-2300 LOCAL). WI AN AREA DEFINED AS 133709N1445205E (UNZ037012.6) TO 133859N1445156E (UNZ032014) THEN CLOCKWISE ON A 1.78NM ARC CENTERED ON 133709N1445205E (UNZ037012.6) TO 133725N1445356E (UNZ042014) TO POINT OF ORIGIN 500FT MSL-12000FT MSL EFFECTIVE 2611160830 UTC (1830 LOCAL 11/16/26) UNTIL 2611211830 UTC (0430 LOCAL 11/22/26) DLY 0830-1830 (1830-0430 LOCAL). WI AN AREA DEFINED AS 133709N1445205E (UNZ037012.6) TO 133859N1445156E (UNZ032014) THEN CLOCKWISE ON A 1.78NM ARC CENTERED ON 133709N1445205E (UNZ037012.6) TO 133725N1445356E (UNZ042014) TO POINT OF ORIGIN 500FT MSL-12000FT MSL EFFECTIVE 2611202200 UTC (0800 LOCAL 11/21/26) UNTIL 2612201300 UTC (2300 LOCAL 12/20/26) DLY 2200-1300 (0800-2300 LOCAL). THE ABOVE DEFINED AIRSPACE CONTAINS CONTINUOUS MILITARY ACTIVITY WHICH CREATES A SERIOUS HAZARD TO AVIATION. AIRCRAFT FLYING WITHIN THE ABOVE AIRSPACE WILL BE EXPOSED TO DIRECT RADIATION WHICH MAY PRODUCE HARMFUL EFFECTS TO PERSONNEL AND EQUIPMENT. RADIATION IS NOT VISUALLY APPARENT AND SHOULD BE PRESUMED BY ALL PILOTS TO CONTINUOUSLY EXIST. ELIOT GRAY, TEL 719-439-8936, IS THE POINT OF CONTACT. THE GUAM /ZUA/ CERAP, TEL 671-473-1210, IS THE CDN FAC. 2611122200-2612201300"},"valid_until":"2026-12-20T13:00:00Z"}}}
